+SOC exchange MPI workers
+========================
+
+For static CPU SOC HSE06 with ordinary ACE, full q points, full spatial
+support, and an orthogonal symmetry-reduced k mesh, set ``nproc_k`` in
+``&parallel`` to the SCF owner count. Launch additional MPI ranks to assign
+r/rprime exchange blocks to workers. For example, ``nproc_k=4`` with 12 MPI
+ranks retains four SCF owners and uses all twelve ranks for exchange work.
+The total rank count may exceed the full or representative k-point count.
+Workers do not hold SCF wavefunctions or ACE factors. This route currently
+supports static GS only; it does not enable empty-k SCF or RT workers.
+Omitting ``nproc_k`` retains ordinary decomposition.
+
+``exx_worker_tile_divisor`` and ``exx_worker_rprime_groups`` (integers,
+both default 0) belong to ``&functional``. Zero selects automatic layout;
+positive values retain manual control. Negative values are invalid. A
+positive rprime group count must divide the total exchange MPI rank count.
+The selector uses the actual symmetry-reduced r representative count and
+all rprime grid points, independently of k-point ownership. It enumerates
+rank factorizations and minimizes the maximum cumulative grid-pair work,
+then maximizes active ranks; ties use fewer column groups. Row batches and
+column chunks retain the 64 MiB density scratch cap. A zero tile divisor
+follows the selected column group count. This is a work-balance model, not
+a guarantee of optimal communication time. Selected geometry and workload
+are printed in ``WAVE_BATCH_ROWS_COLUMNS_GROUPS`` and
+``WAVE_LAYOUT_R_RPRIME_PEAK_ACTIVE``. Historical worker environment
+variables are not read. Unsupported helper layouts, including band
+unfolding, are rejected before workers enter their loop.
+
+``exx_k_algorithm='auto'`` now selects full spinor pairs for eligible native
+CPU full-q SOC HSE06; unsupported backends retain reference selection.
+Explicit ``reference`` and compatible legacy switches remain available.
+This changes the exchange implementation, not physical approximation
+parameters. The integrated implementation has local GNU MPI regression
+coverage; these tests do not certify large-scale capacity or Fujitsu
+production accuracy/performance.
